WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.320
Previously on How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们是如何创造你母亲的》。

2
00:00:02.320 --> 00:00:06.440
Welcome to the first episode of How We Made Your Mother.
欢迎收看《我们是如何创造你母亲的》第一集。

3
00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.160
Are we calling it Whim-Yim?
我们是在叫它“威姆-伊姆”吗？

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:09.320
I was wondering about that.
我刚才就在想这个。

5
00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:10.160
Whim-Yim.
威姆-伊姆。

6
00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.200
I think it's Whim-Yim.
我觉得是威姆-伊姆。

7
00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:12.120
Does it work?
行得通吗？

8
00:00:12.120 --> 00:00:13.600
I think it does.
我觉得行得通。

9
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.160
I so enjoy talking about how I made your mother with you
我非常喜欢和你一起谈论我是如何创造你母亲的，

10
00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:20.640
and unpacking this thing we made that has been the biggest gift
并剖析我们创造的这个东西，它一直以来都是最大的礼物，

11
00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.160
and has carried a lot of shadow with it.
同时也带着许多阴影。

12
00:00:23.160 --> 00:00:28.240
And it's just like all things is a very complicated thing,
就像所有事情一样，这是一件非常复杂的事，

13
00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:29.800
but also a very beautiful thing.
但也是一件非常美好的事。

14
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.760
And you're the person I love talking about this show with the moSt.
而你是我最喜欢一起谈论这部剧的人。

15
00:00:33.760 --> 00:00:36.560
So when this idea struck me like, you know what?
所以当我突然想到这个主意，你知道吗？

16
00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:39.920
It's actually time for me to turn around and revisit
其实是时候让我转过头来重新审视

17
00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:43.360
how I made your mother, but also watch it a lot of the episodes.
我是如何创造你母亲的，同时也重温很多集。

18
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:45.320
For the first time, I only watched about half the episodes,
起初我只看了大约一半的剧集，

19
00:00:45.320 --> 00:00:46.160
what it was on.
也就是它热播的时候。

20
00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:51.680
So I will be re-watching the show along with you and our listeners,
所以我将和你们以及我们的听众一起重温这部剧，

21
00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:54.040
some of whom I assume will be coming to the show for the first time,
我想其中有些人可能是第一次看这部剧，

22
00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.640
other ones will have watched it many times
另一些人则已经看过很多遍，

23
00:00:55.640 --> 00:00:59.280
and are just looking for the backstage notes here.
只是来这里寻找幕后花絮的。

24
00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.400
But I figured if I'm going to do this, why don't we put it on the record
但我想如果我要这么做，为什么不把它记录下来，

25
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.600
and actually just walk through the show together?
然后一起把这部剧过一遍呢？

26
00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:09.400
And it's much like the older, wiser, narrator tag,
这很像年长、更睿智的旁白设定，

27
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.480
which we are now around that age.
我们现在也到了那个年纪。

28
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:15.520
Let's look back and see who we were, who we are now, where we're going.
让我们回过头来看看我们曾经是谁，现在是谁，我们要去向何方。

29
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.880
And yeah, what else would you say about what we're doing here?
还有，是的，关于我们在这里做的事情，你还会说些什么？

30
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:21.360
Well, first of all, I can't believe we only watched half the episodes.
首先，我真不敢相信我们只看了半数剧集。

31
00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:22.280
I'm deeply offended.
我深受打击。

32
00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:23.680
I think I'm just going to walk off.
我想我直接走开算了。

33
00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:24.800
I'm walking off the project.
我要退出这个项目了。

34
00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.160
I'm alone.
我独自一人。

35
00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:46.547
Hello.
你好。

36
00:01:46.547 --> 00:01:50.690
Welcome to season four of how we made your mother.
欢迎收看《我们是如何创造你母亲的》第四季。

37
00:01:50.690 --> 00:01:52.386
I'm here with my friend Craig Thomas.
我和我的朋友克雷格·托马斯在这里。

38
00:01:52.386 --> 00:01:52.890
Hey, Craig.
嘿，克雷格。

39
00:01:52.890 --> 00:01:54.104
Hey there, Josh.
嘿，乔什。

40
00:01:54.104 --> 00:01:55.090
Welcome back.
欢迎回来。

41
00:01:55.090 --> 00:01:55.554
Yeah, man.
是啊，老兄。

42
00:01:55.554 --> 00:01:57.130
It's going to be back season four.
第四季回归了。

43
00:01:57.130 --> 00:01:58.469
How are we here already?
我们怎么就已经到这里了？

44
00:01:58.469 --> 00:01:59.250
This is crazy.
这太疯狂了。

45
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:04.090
Well, that we, Alec, just treated us to a little flashback
好吧，艾力克刚才带我们回顾了一下

46
00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:07.570
to the beginning of our flashback podcast about a show
我们的闪回播客的开头，关于一部剧，

47
00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:09.970
that's a flashback within a flashback within a flashback,
它是一层套一层的闪回，就像俄罗斯套娃一样。

48
00:02:09.970 --> 00:02:11.730
like so many Russian nesting dolls.
就像这样。

49
00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:13.490
It's how I met your mother.
这就是《老爸老妈浪漫史》。

50
00:02:13.490 --> 00:02:15.490
I think this is the best way to say that.
我觉得这是最好的表达方式。

51
00:02:15.490 --> 00:02:18.050
And now I'm getting off, walking off the project again.
现在我又开始发飙、再次退出这个项目了。

52
00:02:18.050 --> 00:02:20.050
It should have been a salmon jam.
本来应该是一场三文鱼果酱的。

53
00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.890
Well, thanks for joining us.
谢谢你们加入我们。

54
00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:24.690
We have missed you.
我们很想念你们。

55
00:02:24.690 --> 00:02:25.650
We've missed each other.
我们也想念彼此。

56
00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.450
It's been a little bit since we've been away.
我们离开了一小段时间。

57
00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:29.250
You've been traveling.
你一直在旅行。

58
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:31.490
You've been doing all kinds of globe trotting.
你一直在进行各种环球旅行。

59
00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.290
And yes, you've had a much more exciting summer than I did.
没错，你的夏天比我精彩得多。

60
00:02:34.290 --> 00:02:39.890
But today we're talking about episode one of season four,
但今天我们要聊的是第四季的第一集，

61
00:02:39.890 --> 00:02:42.770
which is called Do I Know You?
名叫《我认识你吗？》。

62
00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:43.214
Yeah.
是的。

63
00:02:43.214 --> 00:02:45.170
And it was written by,
它是……如果我没记错的话，

64
00:02:45.170 --> 00:02:48.690
quick me if I'm wrong here, Carter Bays and Craig Thomas,
是由卡特·贝斯和克雷格·托马斯写的，

65
00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:49.170
I believe.
我没记错吧。

66
00:02:49.170 --> 00:02:49.730
Cart hair.
卡特·黑尔。

67
00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.250
It's been as a Cart hair base.
一直是卡特·黑尔·贝斯。

68
00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:51.810
Cart hair base.
卡特·黑尔·贝斯。

69
00:02:51.810 --> 00:02:53.730
Cart hair base.
卡特·黑尔·贝斯。

70
00:02:53.730 --> 00:02:54.370
We wrote this.
我们写了这个。

71
00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:55.650
Yeah, we wrote a lot of the premieres.
是的，我们写了很多首播集。

72
00:02:55.650 --> 00:02:57.250
We tended to just come and feel like, all right,
我们往往会直接来到现场，心想：好吧，

73
00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:58.130
let's set the tone.
让我们定下基调。

74
00:02:58.130 --> 00:02:59.090
Let's come in and kind of get it going.
让我们切入正题并让它运转起来。

75
00:02:59.090 --> 00:03:00.530
I don't think it was a premiere episode
我想没有哪一集首播集

76
00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:01.650
that you didn't write.
不是你写的。

77
00:03:01.650 --> 00:03:02.610
I think that's right.
我想是的。

78
00:03:02.610 --> 00:03:03.250
I think that's right.
我想是这样的。

79
00:03:03.250 --> 00:03:04.610
And if there is, I will be surprised.
如果有的话，我会很惊讶。

80
00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.210
And I think we wrote all the premieres.
我觉得所有的首播集都是我们写的。

81
00:03:06.210 --> 00:03:06.770
Yeah.
是的。

82
00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:09.090
I will say my first note right off the bat.
我要说，我一上来想到的第一个意见是：

83
00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:10.770
It shouldn't have been called Do I Know You?
它不应该叫《我认识你吗？》。

84
00:03:10.770 --> 00:03:12.370
That's too forgettable of a title.
这个名字太容易让人遗忘了。

85
00:03:12.370 --> 00:03:15.730
It should have been called something like the Star Wars TeSt.
它应该叫类似《星球大战测试》这样的名字。

86
00:03:15.730 --> 00:03:18.130
Because that's the thing people remember from this episode.
因为那是人们对这一集的记忆点。

87
00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.490
It's the Star Wars TeSt.
这就是《星球大战测试》。

88
00:03:19.490 --> 00:03:21.090
Does this woman like Star Wars?
这个女人喜欢《星球大战》吗？

89
00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:22.290
I think we right off the bat.
我觉得我们一开始……

90
00:03:22.290 --> 00:03:26.130
Well, I would argue that Do I Know You,
好吧，我要说《我认识你吗？》虽然表面上看起来很泛泛，

91
00:03:26.130 --> 00:03:28.530
while it might seem on its face to be generic,
但实际上它既关乎A故事，也关乎B故事。

92
00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:31.330
actually pertains to the A and B story both.
确实如此。

93
00:03:31.330 --> 00:03:31.890
It does.
不，它从主题上看是行得通的。

94
00:03:31.890 --> 00:03:33.570
No, it works like thematically.
但每当我看到《我认识你吗？》这个标题，

95
00:03:33.570 --> 00:03:35.570
But when I see the title, Do I Know You?
我就会想：那一集到底是哪一集来着？

96
00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.090
I go, which one was that again?
哦，就是《星球大战测试》那一集。

97
00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:38.690
Oh, it's the Star Wars Test one.
就是我想让它喜欢《星球大战》的那一集。

98
00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.930
It's the one where I want to tell it to like Star Wars.
这就好比《老友记》的剧名起得很好，

99
00:03:40.930 --> 00:03:42.850
And that's where like the Friends titles were good,
因为这正是你思考的方式……

100
00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:45.010
because it is kind of how you think about like,
因为这有点像是你的想法，比如说，

101
00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:46.370
what's the thing you think about?
你最在意的是什么？

102
00:03:46.370 --> 00:03:48.530
But I would say some of this Monday morning quarterback
不过我要说，我们现在做的这些马后炮式的分析，

103
00:03:48.530 --> 00:03:50.450
we're doing, especially around titles,
尤其是关于剧名的，

104
00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:53.330
is because you saw what stuck from the episode.
是因为你看到了那一集里什么内容留了下来。

105
00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:53.810
Right.
对吧。

106
00:03:53.810 --> 00:03:54.450
That's that.
就是这样。

107
00:03:54.450 --> 00:03:54.850
Thank you.
谢谢。

108
00:03:54.850 --> 00:03:57.570
That's a very generous take to our past selves.
这对我们过去的自己来说已经很宽容了。

109
00:03:57.570 --> 00:03:59.570
And that is the part that stuck.
而这就是留下来的一部分。

110
00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:01.810
There's like lots of memes from this episode.
这一集里有很多梗。

111
00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:03.010
Ted watching Star Wars.
泰德在看《星球大战》。

112
00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:05.330
Star Wars is a thing.
《星球大战》是一回事。

113
00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:06.050
That's the thing.
就是这样。

114
00:04:06.050 --> 00:04:06.770
That's the thing.
就是这样。

115
00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:09.410
And there's like little meme to moments that fans send
这一集里还有粉丝们发来的很多小梗，

116
00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:11.730
from this episode that we'll get to.
我们一会儿会聊到。

117
00:04:11.730 --> 00:04:13.250
And so yes, that became the thing.
所以，是的，这就成了那个梗。

118
00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:13.810
But you're right.
但你说得对。

119
00:04:13.810 --> 00:04:16.690
You don't know in the moment that that's going to stick,
你在当时并不知道这会流传开来，

120
00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.530
you know, how many years later?
你知道的，那是多少年之后了？

121
00:04:18.530 --> 00:04:19.410
Alec, when did this air?
亚历克，这是什么时候播出的？

122
00:04:19.410 --> 00:04:20.370
This is a good moment to us.
这对我们来说是个好问题。

123
00:04:20.370 --> 00:04:21.490
How many years later are we?
我们是隔了多少年？

124
00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.450
Hey guys, this aired on September 20.
嘿，伙计们，这是在9月20日播出的。

125
00:04:24.450 --> 00:04:25.010
Hi.
嗨。

126
00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:25.490
Hi, Greg.
嗨，格雷格。

127
00:04:25.490 --> 00:04:26.210
Hi, Josh.
嗨，乔希。

128
00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:29.570
This aired on September 22, 2008.
这是在2008年9月22日播出的。

129
00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:31.250
Okay.
好的。

130
00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:33.890
So when we last left our heroes,
那么，当上次我们离开我们的主角时，

131
00:04:35.090 --> 00:04:39.010
Ted was jammed into a little booth at an arcade.
泰德被挤在游戏厅的一个小隔间里。

132
00:04:39.490 --> 00:04:41.410
Proposing to Stella.
向斯特拉求婚。

133
00:04:41.410 --> 00:04:42.770
It was kind of cliffhanger, right?
这算是一个悬念，对吧？

134
00:04:42.770 --> 00:04:44.530
He asked, he says, Will you marry me?
他问，他说，你愿意嫁给我吗？

135
00:04:44.530 --> 00:04:46.850
I think that's the last words of the season.
我想那是这一季的最后几句话。

136
00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.330
Yeah.
对。

137
00:04:47.330 --> 00:04:50.370
That is that we stopped mid-sentence for the second time
那是我们在这部剧里第二次

138
00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:51.330
in series at this point.
在句子中间戛然而止。

139
00:04:51.330 --> 00:04:53.730
We also started, we stopped mid-word
我们在第二季和第三季之间

140
00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:56.530
between season two and season three in the middle
也在单词中间停了下来，停在

141
00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:57.490
of the word legendary.
“legendary”（传奇）这个词的中间。

142
00:04:57.490 --> 00:05:00.370
It was a cliffhanger halfway through a word.
那是一个卡在一个词中间的悬念。

143
00:05:00.370 --> 00:05:02.930
And this is a cliffhanger halfway through a question
而这是一个卡在一个问题中间的悬念，

144
00:05:02.930 --> 00:05:04.050
that we're waiting for the answer.
我们在等待答案。

145
00:05:04.050 --> 00:05:04.210
Yeah.
对。

146
00:05:04.210 --> 00:05:07.170
But the beginning of episode one of season four,
但是在第四季第一集的开头，

147
00:05:08.050 --> 00:05:10.770
they're directly, we're back in that arcade.
他们直接回到了那个游戏厅。

148
00:05:10.770 --> 00:05:11.330
Right there.
就在那里。

149
00:05:11.330 --> 00:05:11.410
Yeah.
对。

150
00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.170
So my memory is we shot the beginning of season four
所以我的记忆是，我们在第三季结束时

151
00:05:15.170 --> 00:05:17.650
at the beginning of, at the end of season three, right?
顺便拍了第四季的开头，对吧？

152
00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.530
Because we had Sarah, we had no one's hairs different,
因为莎拉在，没有人的发型变了，没有人的……

153
00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:21.010
no one's.
对。

154
00:05:21.010 --> 00:05:21.570
Yeah.
我两季之间

155
00:05:21.570 --> 00:05:23.410
I didn't gain an enormous amount of weight
也没有胖得离谱。

156
00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:26.130
in between the two seasons.
对。

157
00:05:26.130 --> 00:05:26.610
Yeah.
所以我确实记得必须在第三季结束时

158
00:05:27.650 --> 00:05:32.770
So what I do remember having to write the beginning of episode
写第四季第一集的开头。

159
00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:35.010
of season four at the end of season three.
我真的，真的不记得了。

160
00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:36.290
I really, really don't.
但我们当时肯定就是这么做的，对吧？

161
00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.130
But that must be what we did, right?
我们不会，我想我们不会把那个布景拆了，

162
00:05:38.130 --> 00:05:41.010
We wouldn't, I don't think we would have dismantled that set
